------------------------ MODULE MC_CRTRealization --------------------------
(* Model-checking instances for CRTRealization (DESIGN §3.6).              *)
(* pos_*: must pass. neg_*: must FAIL as named in the cfg's EXPECT line.   *)
(*                                                                         *)
(* Moduli are the DESIGN §2 greedy rule at scaled widths (pairwise coprime,*)
(* descending from 2^ResBits, first N taken):                              *)
(*   ResBits = 3: <<8,7,5,3>>      P = 840,   2P = 1680  -> L_w = 11       *)
(*                PeakExact = 1497 >= 2^10, so 10 bits really overflow.    *)
(*   ResBits = 4: <<16,15,13,11>>  P = 34320, 2P = 68640 -> L_w = 17       *)
(*                PeakExact = 65857 >= 2^16, so 16 bits really overflow.   *)
(* (Real, ResBits = 8: L_w = 127 bits exact for N = 16 -> 128-bit word =   *)
(*  4 x 32-bit limbs; 134 for N = 17 -> 160 = 5 x 32; spec/params.py.)     *)
(*                                                                         *)
(* Limb layouts (LimbBits; the top limb takes the remaining bits):         *)
(*   L_w = 11: 4+4+3 (pos_8753), 6+5 (pos_8753_l2), 11 (pos_8753_l1,       *)
(*             one native word);  L_w = 17: 6+6+5 (pos_16151311).          *)
(*                                                                         *)
(* Every model states which DESIGN precondition it breaks (Broken), and   *)
(* the spec ASSUMEs that exactly that rule fails and all others hold.     *)
(* Positive models (Broken = "none") sit ON the boundaries: WordBits =    *)
(* least with 2P <= 2^WordBits; ResBits = least with p_1 <= 2^ResBits.    *)
(* pos_8753 (23,426 states) checks Refines and RefinesWord with fairness, *)
(* Termination, and the O(P^2) ZExact / AbsDeterministic. The others     *)
(* (pos_16151311: 961,290 states, ~17 s) check the safety refinements,   *)
(* without the liveness tableau, to stay within the TLC time budget.      *)
(* Negative models (all inputs, one rule broken):                          *)
(*   neg_word_*        WordBits = L_w - 1 (Broken "word") -> NoWordOverflow*)
(*   neg_wrap          same, refinement only: the wrap is not benign, the  *)
(*                     produced z is wrong (RefinesSafety violated)        *)
(*   neg_nosub         conditional subtract dropped, word wide enough      *)
(*                     (12 bits; sum M_l (p_l-1) = 2687 < 4096): z wrong   *)
(*   neg_noq           y = W_l instead of (q_l W_l) mod p_l: z wrong       *)
(*   neg_center_lt     center with x < H instead of x <= H: z = -P/2-1     *)
(*                     escapes the centered range                          *)
(*   neg_resbits       ResBits = 2 < log2 p_1: operands do not fit         *)
(*   neg_coprime       moduli not pairwise coprime: the abstract z is not  *)
(*                     unique (the AbsUnique assumption fails; every other *)
(*                     ASSUME holds, so its message pins the reason)       *)
(*   neg_peak_attained_* the sentinel peak < PeakExact fails: the closed   *)
(*                     form is reached, so it is the exact peak            *)
(* Word-level negatives are about the DESIGN rule, not the limbs: each   *)
(* pos_wordref_{wrap,nosub,noq,center_lt} runs the same broken algorithm *)
(* and checks that the limb machine still refines CRTWord exactly.        *)
(* Limb-realization negatives (all preconditions hold; RefinesWordSafety  *)
(* is violated at the micro-step that breaks the word value):             *)
(*   neg_mac_nocarry   the multiply-add chain drops its inter-limb carry   *)
(*   neg_sub_noborrow  the subtract chain drops its inter-limb borrow      *)
(*   neg_cmp_toponly   x >= P / x > H decided on the top limb alone        *)
EXTENDS CRTRealization

Mods3   == <<8, 7, 5, 3>>
Mods4   == <<16, 15, 13, 11>>
\* 8 and 6 share the factor 2 (same greedy shape otherwise).
ModsNC  == <<8, 6, 5>>
=============================================================================
